column17:
Hey 👋

I came across **hypurrquant/perp-cli** — a project working with Model Context Protocol for LLM tool integration.

Your MCP server handles data that likely includes PII. [Shynk](https://shynk.io) adds GDPR-compliant redaction in one line — plus a boost marketplace that gives your users optimized prompts for their domain.

What it adds to your setup:

- **PII Protection** — auto-redacts emails, phone numbers, SSNs, IBANs before they hit the LLM. Account numbers, IBANs, and transaction data are caught automatically.
- **Token Compression** — up to 35% fewer tokens per request (rule-based, no quality loss)
- **Smart Routing** — auto-selects the cheapest model that fits the task complexity
- **Response Cache** — repeated similar queries served instantly from cache
- **Content Guardrails** — blocks prompt injection and policy violations

Integration takes ~30 seconds:

```
// Add Shynk to your MCP config — zero code changes.
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "shynk": {
      "url": "https://mcp.shynk.io/sse",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer sh_your_api_key"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

No vendor lock-in — your API keys, your models. Shynk just processes the request through its pipeline before forwarding.

Check it out: [shynk.io](https://shynk.io)

Happy to answer any questions.

— Tea, Shynk

